  "description": "The canonical Qwen-Image serve layout: the diffusers QwenImageTransformer2DModel, all-bf16, every declaration derived from the real safetensors headers of the hub trees the fleet ACTUALLY SERVES - tensorhub/qwen-image (sha256:0780e58ef8ec..., QwenImagePipeline) and tensorhub/qwen-image-edit-2511 (sha256:53058727d177..., QwenImageEditPlusPipeline). ONE DOCUMENT COVERS BOTH REPOS, and that is a measurement rather than a judgement call: the two transformers are 1933 tensors each, the name sets are equal (zero keys unique to either side), every shared shape agrees and every dtype agrees. Both transformer/config.json declare _class_name QwenImageTransformer2DModel with num_layers 60, attention_head_dim 128, num_attention_heads 24, axes_dims_rope [16, 56, 56] and joint_attention_dim 3584; the only config delta is zero_cond_t on the edit arm, a forward-pass flag that is not a tensor. The two serve on two pipeline classes and two compiled cells (pgw#1112), but a compile-cell split is not a layout split. Same one-root precedent as wan22.diffusers-bf16. COMPLETENESS IS LOAD-BEARING ON THIS FAMILY SPECIFICALLY. flux2-klein.diffusers-bf16@1 already explains 722 of these 1933 keys (37.4%, measured) because both families serve the diffusers MMDiT spelling - transformer_blocks.{i}.attn.to_q/to_k/to_v, add_*_proj, norm_added_*, to_add_out. Detection specificity is the count of a file's tensors a contract explains, so a SAMPLED qwen document would lose qwen's own files to flux2-klein. This declaration is COMPLETE over the shipped header: all 1933 keys, no exceptions. ATTENTION IS SPLIT ON BOTH STREAMS, NOT FUSED. The image stream is to_q/to_k/to_v at [3072, 3072] with [3072] biases; the text stream is add_q_proj/add_k_proj/add_v_proj at the same ranks. No fusion is declared because no shipped packaging fuses, but the roles carry #q/#k/#v suffixes over one qkv role so a future fused [9216, 3072] packaging - equal thirds here, measured - is a run-preserving derive rather than a refusal, exactly as the sdxl.clip-g-* pair does. NOTE THE CONTRAST WITH FLUX.2 KLEIN, because the shared spelling invites the wrong assumption: Klein's single_transformer_blocks.{i}.attn.to_qkv_mlp_proj fuses attention AND a GATED mlp at 1:1:1:6, and thirds would mis-cut it. Qwen has no such tensor at all - its img_mlp/txt_mlp are plain non-gated 4x MLPs shipped already split (net.0.proj at [12288, 3072], net.2 at [3072, 12288]). img_mod.1/txt_mod.1 at [18432, 3072] are 6 x 3072 adaLN modulation, which no packaging splits, so they are declared whole. TRANSFORMER ONLY, deliberately, on the tensorfs#121 rule: AutoencoderKLQwenImage and the Qwen2.5-VL text encoder are undeclared. DO NOT ADD THE VAE LATER: AutoencoderKLQwenImage is NOT qwen-only - internvl-U ships the same VAE class (measured by the vlm lane, se#769 wave-3), so declaring it here would tie family detection ACROSS family lines, not merely within this one. That is the tensorfs#122 regression reached from two directions at once, and it is the reason this exclusion is written down rather than left implicit - a shared component makes family detection TIE (tensorfs#122), and the encoder spelling is stock transformers that any future Qwen2.5-VL lane would collide with. The transformer is the compile subject and the only component that identifies the family. Per-tensor dtypes are a MEASURED HISTOGRAM, not the hub row's advertised scalar: both served transformers count 1933 BF16 and 0 of anything else. A hub row's flat dtype field is an advertisement; a structured minority set (a trailing block, norm_out/proj_out) is a real and observed failure mode elsewhere in the fleet, so it was counted here rather than assumed. Top-level dtype is the serve-side load dtype (ctx.lane.dtype); the per-tensor dtypes are the matcher's constraint that this really is the bf16 packaging.",
